1.Core Data Model & Policy Configuration
User Story1: Creation of custom objects
*Go to setup, Click on object Manager.
Click on create and select custom object.
Fill the following details:
Label: Policy
Plural Label: Policies
Object Name: Auto Populated
Record Name: Policy Number
Data type: Auto Number
Format: P - {0000}
Starting Number: 1
Under optional features:
Allow Reports, Activities and Track field History
Under Deployment Status:
Select the deployed radio button.
Under Search Status:
Check the Allow Search checkbox.
Click on save.

2.Define Record Types on Policy Object:
*Go to setup, Click on Object Manager.
○ Search for Policy objects and click on Policy__c.
○ In the left side panel, click on the record types.
○ Click on New.
○ Fill out the following details:
○ Select the existing record type as Master.
○ Give record type label as “Auto”
○ Record Type Name will be auto populated.
○ Give a meaningful description.
○ Check the active checkbox.
○ Check the Make Available checkbox for all the profiles.
○ Click on Next.
● It will redirect to the Assign page layouts page, Leave everything as is, and click on save

3.Create Field Sets for policy specific data:

*Go to setup, Click on Object Manager.
Search for Policy object and click on Policy__c.
In the left side panel, click on the Field Sets.
Click on New.
Fill out the following details:
Field Set Label as Vehicle
Field Set Name will be Auto populated.
Where is this used: In the policy object.
Click on save.
Click on the field set you have just created and it will redirect to the page layout setup.
Drag VIN, and model year fields to the field set and click on save.

